{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"c046f851da2b0bc2521c808d0dd04dddc36ffbcb39125b62f6aa1590f64453af","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_59622851fa0c803a56c87a7dc16a113cf1c29f87c3676b3d7b21af3e6c0be795","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a significant methodological contribution to semi-supervised learning by introducing self-ensembling, which leverages the stochastic nature of dropout and augmentation to generate pseudo-labels. The reported results demonstrate substantial improvements over prior state-of-the-art methods on standard benchmarks, accompanied by a useful analysis of robustness to label noise. The simplicity and efficiency of the proposed temporal ensembling approach suggest high potential for adoption and further research in the field.","paper_id":"BJ6oOfqge","paper_identity_sha256":"fb86245df0c3c1cd87423f48d29c452557dfd466ad41806564274fbd4b6f1eb5","prompt_identity_sha256":"706c3407f1e6a7c4950a7ef1c8562e91d260661f0aa4ac63959ec82b1cc9f1b1","raw_response_sha256":"1d2c8e8c2781e24bc079bd56304f79693fd61750a32129de298092c256bed212","request_identity_sha256":"6468c2de97b5b99c16192af755989fd21f0ada248ab24c87d5a4d984fc77cdf0","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"SIGN","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"4665a6a172d64a89dedcf8e3ec21323ba91ff11a831e10731f470cd8c9c78a9d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-002","SRC-003"],"review_text":"The work addresses the broadly important problem of semi-supervised learning, where labeled data is scarce. By introducing a method that exploits the inherent stochasticity of deep network training (via dropout and augmentation) to form ensemble predictions, the paper offers a generalizable paradigm. This approach is not limited to specific architectures but relies on standard training components, making it likely to influence a wide range of researchers working on data-efficient learning and regularization techniques.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-BRD"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-015","SRC-016","SRC-017"],"review_text":"The paper demonstrates strong domain impact within computer vision, specifically for image classification tasks on CIFAR-10 and SVHN. The method significantly reduces classification error rates in low-label regimes (e.g., 500 or 4000 labels), which is a critical challenge in practical applications where labeling is expensive. The reported improvements over supervised-only baselines and previous semi-supervised methods indicate that the technique is effective for the specific domain of small-scale image classification.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-DOM"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-018","SRC-019"],"review_text":"The paper reports substantial improvements over the state of the art. On CIFAR-10 with 4000 labels, the error rate is reduced from 18.63% (Salimans et al.) to 16.55% (Pi-model) and 12.16% (Temporal Ensembling with augmentation). On SVHN with 500 labels, the error rate drops from 18.44% to 5.12%. These gains are consistent across multiple runs (10 runs reported) and are statistically significant given the low standard deviations. The method also outperforms supervised-only baselines when all labels are available, suggesting a robust advantage over previous approaches.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-SOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-020","SRC-022"],"review_text":"The paper highlights a practical benefit regarding robustness to incorrect labels. Figure 2 and Section 3.4 demonstrate that the Pi-model maintains high classification accuracy even when a significant portion of the training labels are randomized, whereas standard supervised training degrades rapidly. This tolerance to label noise is a valuable property for real-world datasets where annotation errors are common, suggesting potential societal and practical benefits in reducing the cost and risk associated with data labeling.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"ebfacad91f48ed6e4a99f33b059b1d38fefdb306b05486ef5a35f1a125a05913","paper_id":"BJ6oOfqge","paper_ordinal":21,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"1d2c8e8c2781e24bc079bd56304f79693fd61750a32129de298092c256bed212","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"BJ6oOfqge","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"73b6f2e94fce86acf14e1345af77c704f069225a1ed0a39a07a4a0e78bde7ad7","request_identity_sha256":"6468c2de97b5b99c16192af755989fd21f0ada248ab24c87d5a4d984fc77cdf0","role":"SIGN","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":802,"prompt_tokens":15090,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":15892},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"6468c2de97b5b99c16192af755989fd21f0ada248ab24c87d5a4d984fc77cdf0","role":"SIGN","role_ordinal":2,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}